## Why This Is Asked

This question probes practical privacy-by-design in streaming: data residency, per-tenant cryptography, access control, auditing, and testability under burst traffic. It also checks operational thinking for cross-tenant isolation and retention policies.

## Key Concepts

- Per-tenant residency and tenancy isolation
- Envelope encryption with KMS and tenant-scoped keys
- Field-level redaction during transit and at rest
- Region routing and data locality guarantees
- Auditing, retention, and compliance controls
- Canary-based validation under burst load and failure scenarios

## Code Example

```javascript
function redact(record, schema) {
  const redacted = {};
  for (const [k, v] of Object.entries(record)) {
    if (schema.redact?.includes(k)) redacted[k] = "***";
    else redacted[k] = v;
  }
  return redacted;
}
```

